[{"id":3330940683,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Gih8L","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While reducing the effects of `ClassDB` on compile time performance is a great goal, I'm not sure about the approach taken here (and the previous PR). I think this becomes more clear when we think about the implications of merging this PR:\r\n\r\nIf we decide the eventual goal is to remove automatic inclusion of the binding methods from the headers, we'll have to accept that every single `.cpp` file for an `Object` subclass that binds methods (i.e. all of them?) will have to include the binder headers explicitly.\r\nFrom a quick glance, that's 900 files. That's a lot of work, and a lot of added includes. And in the end, every single Object subclass `.cpp` file will still include `ClassDB` because it needs to register its bindings to it. There might be some compile units that no longer need to include `ClassDB`, but I have a feeling it wouldn't be enough to be worth it.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, that makes the `ClassDB` include problem a 